Drop the last two `maxHeartbeats 0` uses: PtfsShaFinal and CutMainCpt.

`set_option maxHeartbeats 0` turns off Lean's time limit for a declaration.
After 0003 two uses were left, and neither is needed. Measured by compiling
each file with different limits after building its dependencies (about 1,950
modules, all of which compiled):

  shaDictFS (PtfsShaFinal.lean)    fails at 1,250,000, passes at 1,500,000
  cpt_copy_thms (CutMainCpt.lean)  passes at 200,000

The project limit in lakefile.toml is 4,000,000, so both now run under it with
more than 2.6 times headroom. With this patch no proof in lean/src turns off
the time limit. Nothing else in the files changes.

